# Single-page app: every path is handled by the client router, so anything the
# server has no file for must return index.html with a 200 rather than a 404.
# Without this, /stats and a shared /results/:id link are dead on arrival.
#
# Read by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages. GitHub Pages ignores it and uses the
# 404.html the build writes instead; nginx and Apache need their own rule — see
# the README.
/*  /index.html  200
